From: RockOS <rockos@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] cage: advertise wayland-drm protocol for EGL buffer sharing

cog (WPE WebKit launcher) uses eglCreateWaylandBufferFromImageWL from
Mesa's EGL_WL_create_wayland_buffer_from_image extension to convert its
exported EGL images into wl_buffers. Mesa only exposes that extension
when the compositor advertises the wayland-drm protocol global (and the
render GPU == display GPU).

wlroots provides wlr_drm_create() for exactly this, but cage never
calls it — so any client relying on the extension (cog/WPE) aborts with:
  on_export_wl_egl_image: assertion failed: (s_eglCreateWaylandBufferFromImageWL)

Register the protocol right after the compositor is created.

--- a/cage.c
+++ b/cage.c
@@ -35,6 +35,7 @@
 #include <wlr/types/wlr_compositor.h>
 #include <wlr/types/wlr_cursor.h>
 #include <wlr/types/wlr_data_device_manager.h>
+#include <wlr/types/wlr_drm.h>
 #include <wlr/types/wlr_export_dmabuf_manager_v1.h>
 #include <wlr/types/wlr_gamma_control_v1.h>
 #include <wlr/types/wlr_idle_inhibit_v1.h>
@@ -405,6 +406,13 @@ main(int argc, char *argv[])
 		goto end;
 	}

+	/* Advertise wayland-drm so Mesa clients can use
+	 * EGL_WL_create_wayland_buffer_from_image (needed by cog/WPE). */
+	if (!wlr_drm_create(server.wl_display, server.renderer)) {
+		wlr_log(WLR_ERROR, "Unable to create the wayland-drm interface");
+		ret = 1;
+		goto end;
+	}
+
 	if (!wlr_subcompositor_create(server.wl_display)) {
 		wlr_log(WLR_ERROR, "Unable to create the wlroots subcompositor");
 		ret = 1;
